This project is an academic-writing extension layered on top of:

  blader/humanizer  (https://github.com/blader/humanizer)
  Copyright (c) 2025 Siqi Chen — MIT License

This distribution includes the upstream base patterns in vendor/ at pinned
commit 9600f2b7241cb4eed6ad803abee5ea01d67fe8e4, unchanged. The upstream MIT
LICENSE and copyright notice are preserved within that copy. scripts/setup.sh
can restore these files; normal use does not require fetching them again.

The original academic-humanizer project contributed the academic override
layer, composed skill entry point, documentation, examples, and setup script.
This adapted distribution additionally modifies the entry point and academic
rules, adds references/claim-directness.md and agents/openai.yaml, and updates
documentation to support English manuscript review and redundant-hedge checks.
